{"v":"3.0.0","project":{"accession":"PRJEB14602","title":"The oral and skin microbiomes of captive Komodo Dragons are significantly shared with their habitat.","description":"Here we collect saliva, skin, and fecal samples from captive Komodo dragons (V. komodoensis) and other captive varanids (V. olivaceus, V. indicus, V. rudicollis) in the first-ever culture-independent assessment of the varanid microbiome. Environmental samples were also collected to characterize host-environment microbiome sharing. This study adds crucial information to our understanding of captive Komodo dragon microbial ecology.","organism":null,"data_type":"Other","center_name":"University of California San Diego Microbiome Initiative","submission_date":"2016/06/28 00:00","last_update":null},"sample_cols":["accession","title","collection_date","country","region","city","lat","lon","urban_status","urban_context","eligibility_reason","isolation_source","env_broad_scale","env_local_scale","env_medium","host","location_resolution","country_iso2","place_id","location_status","location_method","location_note","geo_loc_raw","collection_year"],"samples":[["SAMEA4051333","1747.200197.holding.pen2.dirt.plant.matter; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)",null,null,null,null,null,null,"uncertain",null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical",null,null,null,null,null,"unknown",null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null],["SAMEA4051334","1747.200197.holding.pen2.straw; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)",null,null,null,null,null,null,"uncertain",null,"conflicting evidence: environmental and host/clinical",null,null,null,null,null,"unknown",null,null,"unresolved",null,null,null,null],["SAMEA4051346","1747.209107.holding.pen.A.debris; Development of the oral microbiota in captive Komodo Dragons (Varanus komodoensis)",null,null,null,null,null,null,"uncertain",null,"conflicting evidence: environmental a